20260527.115858.579 [>kpop..........] ## Definition: Claims vs Hypotheses
20260527.115858.579 [>kpop..........] 
20260527.115858.579 [>kpop..........] - Label uncertain reasoning as Hypothesis; only use Claim with explicit evidence.
20260527.115858.580 [>kpop..........] - Claims must cite evidence (code refs, logs, metrics). Otherwise, downgrade to Hypothesis.
20260527.115858.580 [>kpop..........] - For each Hypothesis, include:
20260527.115858.580 [>kpop..........]   - Hypothesis: concise, falsifiable statement.
20260527.115858.580 [>kpop..........]   - Predictions: measurable outcomes if true.
20260527.115858.580 [>kpop..........]   - Test: minimal experiment (setup, variables, metrics, pass/fail).
20260527.115858.580 [>kpop..........]   - Confounders: likely alternatives and controls.
20260527.115858.580 [>kpop..........] - Language:
20260527.115858.580 [>kpop..........]   - Hypothesis: “suggests”, “may”, “indicates”.
20260527.115858.580 [>kpop..........]   - Claim (with evidence): “shows”, “demonstrates”, “causes”.
20260527.115858.580 [>kpop..........] - Label any statement which is a hypothesis as such.
20260527.115858.580 [>kpop..........] - The use plan,`./.malvin/logs/20260527_155418_yuppmvi0/plan.md`, when present, overrides ADVICE. ADVICE is not binding.
